{
  "name": "Retry Effects · 9 Lab",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "parameters": {
        "content": "## Retry Effects · Lab\nFor measuring, not for production. Each row is one way to make the same call for N items. `POST retryfx/lab/<case>` with `{ \"run\": \"...\", \"items\": 5 }`; the stand-in service is told beforehand which item to fail and how. The tests retry the failed execution and count what the stand-in received.\n\n- `plain`: One HTTP Request node gets all items.\n- `retry-on-fail`: Same, with Retry On Fail on the node (3 tries).\n- `loop`: Loop Over Items, batch size 1, the call inside the loop.\n- `sub`: The call sits in a sub-workflow, behind a step that completes.\n- `check-first`: A ledger check and claim in front of the call, in the same workflow.\n- `guarded`: Each item goes through Guarded call.\n- `guarded-retry-on-fail`: Same, with Retry On Fail on the Execute Sub-workflow node.",
        "width": 760,
        "height": 300,
        "color": 4
      },
      "id": "00770fab-0ae2-4098-85af-318e1138b78e",
      "name": "About",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        -40,
        -360
      ]
    },
